  "description": "An invite of version 2 (PROTOCOL 20.8, ADR 0024): the connect ceremony bound to its secret. Both renderings start with the marker \"9\", which no base32 parser accepts, so a client from before it refuses the invite rather than running version 1. invite_key = HKDF-SHA256(secret, salt=\"\", info=\"z-connect-invite-v2\", 32). Each commitment is HMAC-SHA256(invite_key, \"z-connect-commit-v2:\" || eph || u16be(len(code)) || code || name); the channel key is HKDF-SHA256(dh, salt=invite_key, info=\"z-connect-channel-v2\", 32); the digits are computed as in connect.json under \"z-connect-sas-v2\"; the mailboxes and the rendezvous id as in mailboxes.json and connect.json under \"z-connect-relay-v2:\" and \"z-connect-rendezvous-v2:\". The frames have the same members and lengths as version 1. A party without the secret — the relay carrying the frames — can derive none of these keys, so a frame it substitutes is refused before either side has the other's identity. version_1_of_the_same_inputs records what version 1 computes from the same ephemerals and identities; a client of version 2 computes none of it. The go-ahead tag is derived from the channel key exactly as group.json shows.",
